---
title: A native .tmd document
subtitle: The Taliesin-native source extension
---

This document is authored in `.tmd`, Taliesin's native source extension. The
renderer treats it exactly like a `.qmd` file: the pipeline reads the source
string, so the extension only governs *recognition* (which files the site walker,
the `check` walker, and link rewriting pick up), never rendering.

## A code block

```python
def greet(name: str) -> str:
    return f"Hello from a .tmd file, {name}!"
```

## A callout

::: {.callout-note}
`.qmd` stays accepted, so existing trees keep working; `.tmd` is simply the name
the project now leads with.
:::
